 overwrite it. Replacing or removing the account notifies the owner. `sign.sock` is served only with `-modem-uid`, which must differ from this process's, agentosd's and the local UI's uids. It admits that uid only, has a 10 s read timeout, and returns the settings and digest answers (`sipsign.Handler`), never the password. The realm is recorded from the first `REGISTER` challenge the account can answer, within 30 minutes of setup (`RealmWindow`; setting up again reopens it). Until the owner confirms that realm on the local page, the account signs only `REGISTER` (`sipsign.Account.RegisterOnly`; security R1 on #116). So a bridge taken over during the window can at most keep a registration going under a realm the owner then sees and refuses. It gets no texts, no calls, and no digest answers beyond `REGISTER`. | CRED-1, CRED-7, ADP-12 | Small. |
